  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Prepared FLINT-backed exact QQ Cantor arithmetic now serves the cached public Jacobian boundary: ordinary P+Q, P.double(), and n*P dispatch through native genus-2/3 arithmetic when available, while explicit reference selection and every operation certificate replay the ordinary Python Cantor path. A quiet same-host bench-1 receipt measured the direct 257-bit scalar boundary at 0.632 ms/call versus Magma 2.18-5 at 0.443 ms/call (1.427x); the public operator locally measures 0.711 ms/call and a nontrivial public addition 0.951 ms/call.",
